WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.497
Warning! Warning!

2
00:00:01.497 --> 00:00:06.705
I built this with AI and text to speech, because I can't narrate for shit!

3
00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:11.408
Voyage put out a big update on the fourteenth of November.

4
00:00:11.408 --> 00:00:13.690
I went through it against my own worlds.

5
00:00:13.690 --> 00:00:15.686
Most of it you don't have to touch.

6
00:00:15.686 --> 00:00:19.508
There's one thing worth checking, and it takes a couple of minutes.

7
00:00:20.900 --> 00:00:24.821
Voyage fixed mix-ups between records that share a name.

8
00:00:24.821 --> 00:00:27.887
Here's my own dev world, before I fixed it.

9
00:00:27.887 --> 00:00:29.312
I search for Katana.

10
00:00:29.767 --> 00:00:32.739
There's an item called Katana.

11
00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:36.886
And a trait, also called Katana, that gives you that item.

12
00:00:36.886 --> 00:00:38.347
That's the common case.

13
00:00:38.347 --> 00:00:42.351
A quest with the same title as the trait it rewards is another.

14
00:00:42.351 --> 00:00:46.354
Give every record its own name and the whole problem goes away.

15
00:00:47.767 --> 00:00:51.533
One name per record means Voyage never has to guess which one you meant.

16
00:00:51.533 --> 00:00:56.555
And if your players get the message your selected traits are not available for this story start,

17
00:00:56.555 --> 00:00:57.706
that's not your names.

18
00:00:57.706 --> 00:01:01.838
It's an old saved character from before the update: have them make a fresh one.

19
00:01:03.233 --> 00:01:09.789
The easy way: export your world from Studio and run the little checker, linked in the description.

20
00:01:09.789 --> 00:01:15.810
It only reads the file, and it lists every name used by two kinds of record, traits first.

21
00:01:15.810 --> 00:01:20.025
No Python? Type each trait name into Studio's file tree search.

22
00:01:20.025 --> 00:01:25.176
If an item, ability, quest or person with the same name comes up, that's one.

23
00:01:26.567 --> 00:01:28.241
Rename one side, not both.

24
00:01:28.241 --> 00:01:30.623
I kept the side players see the most.

25
00:01:30.623 --> 00:01:35.258
My creator pick is now Katana Bearer, and it still gives you the Katana.

26
00:01:35.258 --> 00:01:38.606
So the inventory and the story didn't change at all.

27
00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:42.332
Studio won't follow a rename for you.

28
00:01:42.332 --> 00:01:49.894
After renaming a trait, fix everything that names it: its creator category, any other trait that unlocks or excludes it,

29
00:01:49.894 --> 00:01:54.306
your premade characters, the level-up pool, abilities that require it,

30
00:01:54.306 --> 00:01:57.457
and any trigger or script that names it in quotes.

31
00:01:58.867 --> 00:02:01.007
Then save and read Studio's warnings.

32
00:02:01.007 --> 00:02:05.056
If it says references missing, something still points at the old name.

33
00:02:05.056 --> 00:02:07.312
And don't worry about players mid-game.

34
00:02:07.312 --> 00:02:09.163
A rename only reaches new games.

35
00:02:09.163 --> 00:02:11.881
Saves keep playing the version they started on.

36
00:02:13.267 --> 00:02:14.662
The rest is optional.

37
00:02:14.662 --> 00:02:18.916
The card description on the Publish tab has a shorter limit now,

38
00:02:18.916 --> 00:02:22.903
two hundred and sixty characters, but only when you edit it.

39
00:02:23.367 --> 00:02:27.181
Combat Settings has new tiers for abilities characters learn in play,

40
00:02:27.181 --> 00:02:29.447
so you can sort moves into small and big.

41
00:02:29.447 --> 00:02:34.091
There's a new trigger that moves a location, made for things like a travelling ship.

42
00:02:34.091 --> 00:02:36.799
And the name filter moved to Content, Characters.

43
00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:42.979
That's it. The written guide and the checker are linked in the description.

44
00:02:42.979 --> 00:02:46.420
My worlds and lorebooks are at deaththegrim.github.io.

45
00:02:46.867 --> 00:02:50.815
I'm Dreamer. Now go build something weird, and I'll see you next time!

